flowchart TB
  accTitle: Switching from another integration for Autodarts
  accDescr: The integration under its former name, Autodarts, up to version 1.18, is no other tool: update it, and HomeDarts takes over its boards. Every other integration, such as the original HACSAutodarts, Quevinsta's, belese's, Autodarts Local, Autodarts Connect Online, Darts Hub or an MQTT bridge, can stay while you switch, because HomeDarts has a domain of its own, homedarts. Install HomeDarts beside it and add the board, move the automations to the events and blueprints of HomeDarts, then delete the entries of the old integration, remove it in HACS and restart Home Assistant.
  OLD["Your integration<br/>for Autodarts today"] --> WHICH{"Which one<br/>is it?"}
  WHICH -- "Autodarts up to 1.18,<br/>the former name<br/>of HomeDarts" --> TAKE["Update it, and<br/>HomeDarts takes over<br/>its boards"]
  WHICH -- "another one:<br/>HACSAutodarts, Quevinsta,<br/>belese, Autodarts Local,<br/>Connect Online,<br/>Darts Hub, MQTT" --> ADD["Install HomeDarts<br/>beside it and<br/>add the board"]
  ADD --> MOVE["Move the automations<br/>to the events and<br/>blueprints of HomeDarts"]
  MOVE --> DONE["Delete the old entries,<br/>remove it in HACS,<br/>restart"]
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  class TAKE,DONE done
